---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import MediaPlaceholder from '../../components/MediaPlaceholder.astro';
import UpdateForm from '../../components/UpdateForm.astro';
---
<Layout title="Stories & Books">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container hero hero--split">
      <div>
        <h1>Stories are the heart of the Aya &amp; Sura world.</h1>
        <p>Cards can teach a word. Activities can fill an afternoon. Stories are where children get to know the characters. Aya &amp; Sura's book line is being built to give families warm, illustrated stories they can read together and return to.</p>
      </div>
      <MediaPlaceholder label="BOOKS HERO — Aya & Sura reading / story-world illustration" ratio="wide" variant={2} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--surface">
    <div class="container hero hero--split">
      <MediaPlaceholder label="BOOK COVER — Giving Thanks to Allah final cover" ratio="portrait" variant={3} />
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Coming Next</p>
        <h2>Giving Thanks to Allah</h2>
        <p>Aya and Sura spend time with their family, play, wait, imagine and discover how gratitude can live inside ordinary moments. Designed as a gentle illustrated story for family reading, <em>Giving Thanks to Allah</em> expands Aya &amp; Sura beyond cards and into a story children can experience from beginning to end.</p>
        <p class="muted">The book is nearing completion. Final availability, printing and launch details will be announced once production is confirmed.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/books/giving-thanks-to-allah/">Get Book Updates</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--soft">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>A world children can grow with</h2>
      <p>Aya &amp; Sura is not planned as a one-book company. Books are one part of a larger character world that can continue through new stories, monthly adventures, cards, activities and the app. Some stories may focus on Muslim family life and faith. Others can explore friendship, patience, curiosity, responsibility and the everyday problems children recognize.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
